From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ophuscado <postbox@ophuscado.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:26:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] thunderbolt: Add out-of-band protocol adapter
 notifications

On Apple Silicon the PCIe down adapter of the host router does not lead
to a device on the Thunderbolt bus. The PCIe controller behind it is a
separate platform device whose link only trains while a tunnel to the
adapter is active, so it has to be told when that tunnel comes and goes.

Add a small class for such controllers: they register a protocol adapter
for their firmware node, and the host router driver looks it up and
calls its activate and deactivate hooks. Add an NHI hook, tunnel_notify,
which the core calls for every tunnel that starts at the host router
when it becomes active and when it stops being active.

The protocol adapter class is Sven Peter's, from the atcphy-20230219
branch of the Asahi Linux tree, reduced to what is used and moved to the
current class API. The hook replaces that branch's
oob_notify_tunnel_state and is called from tb_tunnel_set_active(), so
that a tunnel which never became active is not reported as gone.

Check: full arm64 build with clang 18, CONFIG_USB4=y, no warnings.
